WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.448
A photo worth a heart? React to it, talk about it, keep it.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:10.802
In the photo view, five quick reactions sit under the photo, with More reactions for

00:00:10.802 --> 00:00:11.616
the rest.

00:00:11.816 --> 00:00:15.694
Tap the heart. The count goes up to ten, and the heart is pressed.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.867
Tap it again, and it is taken back. More reactions offers the others, like a party

00:00:22.867 --> 00:00:23.582
popper.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.811
If a reaction can't be saved, the count goes back to what it was, and a message says

00:00:30.811 --> 00:00:31.283
so.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.038
On a phone, Comment opens Photo comments: oldest first, each with a face, a first

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:40.333
name and a time.

00:00:40.533 --> 00:00:42.916
Add one, and the count goes up to four.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.608
A comment takes up to five hundred characters, and a count shows near the limit.

00:00:50.808 --> 00:00:53.014
With none yet, it invites the first.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.519
Your own comment has Delete. It goes once you confirm.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.873
From ten twenty-four pixels, there is no dialog. The same comments sit beside the

00:01:08.873 --> 00:01:11.158
photo, with the field under them.

00:01:11.358 --> 00:01:13.665
The same comments, in two places.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.333
Save photo downloads it at the size it was added, without location or device data.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.072
Your own photo has Photo actions, and the Host can delete any photo in the album.

00:01:29.272 --> 00:01:33.974
Delete this photo? Once you confirm, you are back in Photos, and it says Photo

00:01:33.974 --> 00:01:34.756
deleted.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.008
In chat, its message now reads Photo removed.

00:01:41.208 --> 00:01:44.678
And anyone looking at it is told This photo was removed.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.716
On a phone, the photo fills the screen, with the react bar under it.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:55.894
From ten twenty-four pixels, the side panel opens beside it.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.975
Once the Popkin wraps up, the reactions and comments stay, to read.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.886
What no screen shows: a deleted photo leaves nothing behind, its reactions and

00:02:12.886 --> 00:02:14.314
comments included.

00:02:14.514 --> 00:02:18.766
Only its author deletes a comment, and a comment's text is never logged.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:24.867
That is journey fourteen. Popkin is a free platform for pop-up communities.
